@* HomePage: the hello-world landing page at "/".

   Presentation only; state and event handling live in HomePage.razor.cs. Every element a test or
   the Puppet tool needs to find carries a stable data-testid, and the data-interactive marker on
   the root element flips to "true" once the live server connection is established so that a
   driver can wait for the page to be clickable instead of guessing with sleeps. *@
@page "/"
@rendermode InteractiveServer

<PageTitle>ReviewCenter</PageTitle>

<main data-testid="home-page" data-interactive="@InteractiveMarker">
    <h1>ReviewCenter</h1>
    <p>Web-based code review for regulated projects.</p>

    <nav>
        <a href="/projects" data-testid="projects-link">Projects</a>
    </nav>

    <section>
        <button type="button" data-testid="hello-button" @onclick="SayHello">Hello</button>
        @if (Greeting is not null)
        {
            <p data-testid="hello-message">@Greeting</p>
        }
    </section>

    <section>
        <button type="button" data-testid="counter-button" @onclick="IncrementCounter">Count</button>
        <p>Count: <span data-testid="counter-value">@Count</span></p>
    </section>
</main>
